 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? That's understandable. One way is to agree with her actively, rather than getting defensive. Let me finish. When she says your place is messy, say something like, Oh, I see how that looks. Then only listen to her criticism about the house. Don't let her bring in personal stuff. That's normal. Keep the conversation focused on the house and maybe agree to make one change before she leaves. Gentlely say you'd really like it her way. Probably not. At that point, you could suggest she keeps her own kitchen and you' keep yours. It' a compromise both can live with. She' probably still criticise, but agreeing and keeping the focus on the kitchen makes it less personal.",
